Where inside the matching the thread is

Run 575's panel said w8m3c2r0d5 AppleARMLightEnLp x0 -|- f- N-.

x0 means the passive match never refused anything, and f- means our own
personality was never turned away at all: it was never offered.  The nub in
that round was called options-common, which is the NVRAM service, so the
matching thread is inside the NVRAM service's matching and the root nub's
matching -- the one our personality belongs to -- has not come round yet.

The thread does not move: m3 has said the same thing for every round since
it was set.  It is inside probeCandidates and it is not in probe(), because
the waypoint before the probe would say 4.

So the waypoints go inside probeCandidates now:

  31  a candidate was taken out of the set
  32  it is a dictionary and not a notifier
  33  about to ask the passive match
  34  the passive match said yes

Which one it stands on is the line it is stuck in.

